From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:18:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] drm/imagination: Support the Apple A10 (T8010) GPU

The A10's GPU is a Rogue core (CORE_ID 0x011b0602, legacy BVNC 13.10.6.2)
whose firmware is Apple's GFX firmware, not Imagination's: it runs on an
RTKit coprocessor, powers the core through Apple's "Fender" block and is
initialized through a host-built memory layout instead of IMG's FWIF.

Add an Apple firmware variant, selected by apple,t8010-gpu and
CONFIG_DRM_POWERVR_APPLE. It keeps powervr's device, GEM, VM and MMU
code and the UAPI, so the GPU appears as an ordinary powervr device, and
replaces what is specific to IMG's firmware:

- power: boot the coprocessor through apple-rtkit, then request Fender
  power state 1 before any RGX register access;
- firmware init: build the init page, memory descriptors and firmware
  contexts (pvr_apple_layout.c) with the kernel VM context's page-table
  root, and wait for the firmware to accept them;
- static device information, as the firmware carries no IMG header;
- no core clock and no RGX interrupt on the AP side.

Compute jobs are queued through the firmware's command and work rings and
complete through a stamp. A bring-up parameter, apple_selftest, runs a
terminate-only job, a shader storing a marker, both in sequence, or the
store in a second GPU VM.
